---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Support" description="Frequently asked questions about ZINNIASHARK and Adequora Writer." path="/support/">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Support</span><h1>Questions, answered simply.</h1><p>Here are a few early answers about Adequora Writer. More documentation will be available as the product approaches release.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container faq">
    <details open><summary>When will Adequora Writer be available?</summary><p>Adequora Writer is currently under development and is planned for distribution through the Microsoft Store. We will publish the download link when it becomes publicly available.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Does Adequora Writer require an account?</summary><p>The product is designed as a local tool and does not require an account, server, or subscription for its core workflow.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Where are my documents stored?</summary><p>Documents are designed to be stored directly on your computer as `.adq` files. You remain responsible for choosing a safe location and maintaining backups.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What can an `.adq` file contain?</summary><p>An `.adq` file can bring together writing, tables, images, audio, and video in one document.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can I use it without an internet connection?</summary><p>Adequora Writer is designed for offline use. Internet access may still be needed for downloading or updating the app through the Microsoft Store.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How can I contact support?</summary><p>Email us at <a href="mailto:contact@zinniashark.com">contact@zinniashark.com</a>. Please do not send passwords or other sensitive information.</p></details>
  </div></section>
</Layout>
